.TH "GLESHA-EXTRACT" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-extract \- unpack an archive into a new directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha extract\fR FILE \-\-into DIR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unpack FILE into DIR, which must not exist. FILE may be an encrypted archive or a compressed tar file; the passphrase is only requested for encrypted input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-into DIR
Unpack into DIR, which must not exist.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha extract documents.tar.xz.gpg \-\-into ~/recovered
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-archive (1),
.BR glesha\-decrypt (1)
